description.narrative:
Output: Cooperation with industry increased and entrepreneurship skills developed 
Indicator: Gender-sensitive multimedia and social media campaign on industry partnerships developed in 2018 and has reached at least 1 million people by 2024 (2017 baseline: 0) 
Achievement: 310626 
Progress/Status: Achieved.
The Project constantly works to raise the public awareness about the PVE and SVE system, MOES KR and SIGSDP activities.
The following mechanisms are used: media stories, programs, interviews, etc.; press tours, press conferences, round tables, etc.; video materials and audio messages; PR events designed to improve the PVE and SVE attractiveness (fairs, festivals, occupational championships, etc.); social networks.
The following information distribution channels were used:
1. National and regional TV stations (UTRK, Ala-Too 24, ELTR, STV, Asia TV);
2. National and regional radio stations (Birinchi radio, Maral VM, Zhamaattyk media, Sputnik);
3. News agencies (Akipress, 24.kg, Sputnik, Kabar.kg, Abal.kg, VB.kg, Azattyk, Kaktus, Europe+, Kut bilim, Vesti);
4. Printed publications (Kut Bilim, Vest, Vecherniy Bishkek);
5. Project and MoES KR websites;
6. Social networks and instant messengers.
By the end of 2022, the total information campaign audience reached 1.124 million people. 
Data Source: Expert council mandate and cooperation agreements, memorandums of understanding, business plans, syllabi, and media items
